WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.210
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.670
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.550
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.720
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.060
My next opponent’s been decided!

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.310
Satoshi has climbed his way
to 64th place in the Hyper Class.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:48.740
His next opponent was none other than
the Galar Gym Leader, Saito.

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:54.370
He had battled Saito twice before,
in the Super Class.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.120
Aqua Break!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.120
Riolu!

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.880
Losing the first match...

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.960
Go!

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:12.260
...and drawing the second match.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.760
Now, their third showdown
has arrived.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:20.440
The decisive battle will take place
on Saito’s home turf,

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.870
in Galar’s Lateral Stadium.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.690
Satoshi and Go have come to see the arena,
to prepare for tomorrow’s battle.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.200
Ms. Saito...

00:01:58.030 --> 00:01:58.860
Halt!

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:03.850
I have not heard from you in some time,
trainer of Riolu.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.610
No, my name’s Satoshi!

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:09.030
And it’s not a Riolu anymore!

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.980
So it has evolved.

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.750
Trainer of Lucario, then.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.540
...Of course.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.310
Oh, right!
Come on out, everyone!

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:42.010
These are my friends.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.540
These six here are my Pokémon.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.970
Six Pokémon each...

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:51.560
So you’ve both seen each other’s hand.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.800
We should train together.

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.910
How about it?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.970
Oh... Sorry.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.370
We’re supposed to
be meeting Corni here.

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:14.010
Corni!

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:22.520
Satoshi...
What if Corni and Ms. Saito...?

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:30.060
She is rather soft,
don’t you think?

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:32.650
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.150
There is no need
for me to say more.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.410
Ms. Saito did say that about her...

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:45.260
Corni said she wanted to see your battle,
but maybe she really intended...

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.500
Corni!

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.480
Corni!

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.520
Saito...

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.940
...kins!

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:41.820
Saito... kins?

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.090
I’m so, so sorry!

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:48.530
They were all sold out
of the Miare Galettes you love!

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:53.000
So... I brought my latest obsession.
Please forgive me!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.000
Oh, was that all?

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.810
You’re not mad?

00:05:59.810 --> 00:06:02.300
That was quite thoughtful of you.
Let’s have some together.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.510
What a relief!

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.210
Hey, weren’t you here
to meet them?

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.640
Oh, hiya, Satoshi!

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:13.390
Hiya...

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.920
Hey, Lucario!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:51.830
Now’s not the time for battling...

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.180
Thanks, Corni.

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:03.280
They all look delighted.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.510
I can’t just bring treats from Kalos
without bringing some Pofflé!

00:07:07.330 --> 00:07:12.120
And <i>these</i> are my current obsession...
Kunoe Chocolat!

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.840
They look great.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.360
Here, you guys try them, too.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.350
I’ll have one!

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:18.670
Me, too!

00:07:18.670 --> 00:07:20.440
Time to eat!

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:23.470
Delicious!

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:25.260
It melts in your mouth...

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:31.260
I could keep eating these forever...

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:35.800
We never would’ve thought
you two were friends.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.100
What? Why not?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:42.780
The first time we battled, Ms. Saito
said you were “rather soft.”

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.400
“She is rather soft,
don’t you think?”

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.240
With this strict look.

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.910
Saitokins is such a sourpuss.

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:51.260
She says battles are to be enjoyed.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.540
But I do not share that sentiment.

00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:56.160
See?

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:59.750
But I don’t mind that side of her.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:03.280
She’s kind to her Pokémon,
and she’s an expert martial artist...

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.260
There’s so much I could learn from her.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:07.990
I could say the same about you, Corni.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:14.010
I love the way you show me
all these tasty sweets!

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:16.350
Wha... The <i>sweets?</i>

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.730
I really enjoyed the Kunoe Chocolat.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:30.840
Hey, this is going to be
the third time you battle, right?

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:35.110
Yeah! I’m looking forward
to our battle, too!

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:37.640
I see this as a trial.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:38.750
A trial...?

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:44.250
Trainer of Lucario, who has
crossed my path three times...

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:49.260
Tomorrow, I believe I’ll find out
what you’re here to show me.

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.760
Yeah. Let’s have a good fight!

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.550
Yes.

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.060
This is gonna be great!

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.110
A showdown between rivals...
I can’t wait!

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:00.410
Can’t tomorrow be here any sooner?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.560
I’ll be cheering you on
with everything I’ve got!

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.900
Cheering for who exactly,
me or Ms. Saito?

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.070
Both of ya!

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.250
This is gonna get tiring...

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:21.250
Ms. Saito was really
fired up back there.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:29.120
I wonder what Pokémon she’ll pick...

00:09:29.120 --> 00:09:31.730
Whoever she picks, I’m gonna win!

00:09:32.930 --> 00:09:34.790
Give it all you’ve got, Satoshi!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.260
Yeah! Thanks for the support, Go.

00:09:46.830 --> 00:09:50.330
The Pokémon World Championships
Hyper Class.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:56.720
Striving to be the world’s strongest Pokémon Trainer,
here we have today’s contenders!

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:01.290
Ranked 30th, a Galar native,
Contestant Saito.

00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:04.030
Equipped with her Daimax Band,
as always!

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.130
Saitokins!

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.230
So she’ll be using Daimax...

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:14.070
Of course! Lateral Stadium’s
a Daimax Power Spot.

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:17.590
And when Saitokins uses Daimax,
it’s a real sight to behold!

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.440
And the trainer who,
in a recent Hyper Class match,

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:25.010
took down Sinnoh’s Contestant Denji
with an astounding Z-Move...

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.910
The one everyone has their eyes on,

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:31.860
Contestant Satoshi from Kanto,
currently ranked 64th!

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:33.180
Satoshi!

00:10:33.180 --> 00:10:34.360
Go for it!

00:10:34.830 --> 00:10:35.700
And what’s this?

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:39.020
The gleaming stone on
Contestant Satoshi’s left hand is a Key Stone.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:42.870
He’s picked Mega Evolution
over Z-Moves, then.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:50.930
Note that in this tournament, you are allowed
one use of either Daimax, Mega Evolution, or a Z-Move.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.760
Mega Evolution...

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.770
Daimax, huh...?

00:11:03.770 --> 00:11:06.770
Today’s battle is a 3v3.

00:11:06.770 --> 00:11:10.770
Mega Evolution and Daimax...
When are they gonna use them?

00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.850
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:17.660
3! 2! 1!

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.160
Go!

00:11:18.160 --> 00:11:19.120
Pikachu... I choose you!
Go!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.340
Pikachu... I choose you!

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.580
Otosupus!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:30.870
Battle, start!

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.380
Lightning Speed!

00:11:33.050 --> 00:11:33.710
Detect!

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:40.930
Electroweb!

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:48.730
All right, it’s trapped!

00:11:49.130 --> 00:11:50.320
Straight for the attack!

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:53.410
So he managed to get
the first hit on Saitokins...

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:56.650
The Lightning Speed was just a feint
for the Electroweb.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:57.880
It had to be!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.660
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:04.620
Infight!
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.840
What?!

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.360
Pikachu!

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.390
An unexpected Infight!

00:12:38.390 --> 00:12:43.490
Completely ignoring the Electroweb,
Otosupus’s display of toughness leaves the crowd gasping!

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.620
The Electroweb...

00:12:50.620 --> 00:12:52.790
Nothing fazes that Otosupus.

00:12:53.280 --> 00:12:54.860
You okay, Pikachu?

00:12:57.920 --> 00:12:59.180
Come back for now!

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.020
Go, Lucario!

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:13.980
Even before it evolved,

00:13:14.910 --> 00:13:17.780
it fought Otosupus to a draw
the last time.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.780
So this is their fateful showdown?

00:13:24.780 --> 00:13:28.350
Lucario! This time we’re gonna
beat that Otosupus!

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.330
Aqua Break!

00:13:34.860 --> 00:13:35.960
Shadow Clones!

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:43.220
Satoshi’s wary of
a close-range battle.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:47.500
I can see why he’d be wary
when Otosupus has Octolock.

00:13:48.310 --> 00:13:50.310
Spin, Otosupus!

00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.060
The Shadow Clones vanish!

00:13:58.060 --> 00:14:01.570
Otosupus used the water spray
from Aqua Break to full effect!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:04.850
But where’s the real Lucario?!

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:06.780
Aura Sphere!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:10.500
Detect!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:14.750
Return, Otosupus!

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.170
Holding off the end for later, huh...?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.690
Oh, they’re just barely getting started.

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:24.580
That was just checking each other out, no?

00:14:24.580 --> 00:14:26.090
Go...

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:28.430
Luchabull!

00:14:33.190 --> 00:14:35.440
Luchabull next, huh?

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:38.250
Contestant Saito’s second pick
is Luchabull.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.320
What kind of battle will it show us?!

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:42.560
Lucario, rush in!

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:45.490
High Jump Kick!

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:51.870
The High Jump Kick hits!

00:14:53.210 --> 00:14:54.160
Wing Attack!

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.470
Lucario!

00:14:59.470 --> 00:15:00.740
Knock back its attacks!

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:03.220
A marvelous exchange of blows!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:06.450
Their speed and power
are evenly matched!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.720
Go!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.360
God Bird!

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:26.860
Force Palm!

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:37.120
Lucario!

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.840
God Bird lands a spectacular blow!

00:15:40.840 --> 00:15:42.710
It must’ve felt that!

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:48.020
She really isn’t giving me
any chance to attack...

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:53.550
That Luchabull’s
even faster than last time.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:55.680
Well, that’s Saitokins for you.

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:58.250
Better today than yesterday,
better tomorrow than today...

00:15:58.250 --> 00:16:00.230
She’s constantly leveling up.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:03.410
The same goes for Satoshi!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.740
All right, you can keep going!

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:15.390
Lucario stands back up!

00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:17.990
What incredible toughness!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.970
Come back, Luchabull.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.590
Go...

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:27.970
Kairiky!

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.830
Contestant Saito’s
third pick is Kairiky!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:38.980
And it arrives with an
oppressive show of determination!

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.990
Kairiky, huh?!

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:49.800
Kairiky! Superstrength Pokémon!
Fighting type!

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:56.420
With four arms that react more quickly than it can think,
it can execute many punches at once!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:00.890
Saitokins is really staying
on the offensive today.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:03.880
She’s already sent out
her true ace!

00:17:03.880 --> 00:17:05.120
Her true ace?!

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:08.630
Of course...
The Daimax Band!

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.510
Bullet Punch!

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:21.560
Force Palm!

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:27.320
A fierce assault by Kairiky!

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:33.970
Rush in again!

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.370
Force Palm!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:41.080
Bullet Punch!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:52.590
Kairiky uses its four arms
to deliver blow after blow!

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:57.600
This is nothing...
This is nowhere near Kairiky’s full strength.

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:05.560
Kairiky immobilizes Lucario!

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:07.020
Cross Chop!

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:16.650
Kairiky is truly fearsome!

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.490
Does Lucario not stand a chance?!

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.000
Bullet Punch!

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:26.830
Lucario!

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:29.420
What will you do now?

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:31.380
Lucario! Contestant Satoshi!

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.580
So strong...

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:38.350
I’d better...

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.310
Huh?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:48.560
What’s this?
Contestant Satoshi brandishes his Mega Glove.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.940
He’s trying to escape his bind
by Mega Evolving?!

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.070
Lucario, let’s go!

00:19:04.070 --> 00:19:06.500
It doesn’t want to Mega Evolve?

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.930
You think so, too?

00:19:08.930 --> 00:19:09.970
Yeah...

00:19:09.970 --> 00:19:11.690
Right, Lucario?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:25.480
Lucario manages
an amazing escape all by itself!

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:26.770
Lucario...

00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:32.970
Lucario’s strong will
suppressed the light from the Key Stone...

00:19:32.970 --> 00:19:34.610
That can happen...?

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:44.500
I got it, Lucario.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:49.420
Contestant Satoshi and Lucario
seem to have fallen apart.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.340
I lost my temper...

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:55.860
I panicked and wasn’t thinking ahead.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:02.440
Pokémon and trainer on equal footing...

00:20:03.880 --> 00:20:05.930
The ideal I aspire to.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.430
Mega Evolution failed to activate!

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:11.900
Was your bond not deep enough,
Contestant Satoshi?!

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:15.070
Far from “not deep enough,”
their bond was perhaps too deep.

00:20:15.730 --> 00:20:17.450
That’s why this happened.

00:20:17.450 --> 00:20:20.070
Champion!
I was getting worried!

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:24.200
Sorry for being late.
Man, I really got lost out there...

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:27.370
What?

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.490
What’s going on?

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:31.540
Whaa?! Mr. Dande?!

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.340
No way! The Champion?!

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:35.590
Mr. Dande!

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:41.660
Their deep bond means
it’ll happen precisely when it’s necessary.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:43.560
That is Mega Evolution.

00:20:43.560 --> 00:20:46.100
But now was not the time.

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:50.100
The Lucario knew,
and stopped its trainer.

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.400
Can’t you feel how close they are?!

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.160
Starting now,
I’ll be joined by today’s special guest,

00:20:57.160 --> 00:21:02.590
the Pokémon World Championships
Monarch, Mr. Dande.

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:04.370
Mr. Dande is watching...

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:08.720
I’m gonna be the one
who battles him!

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.900
No, it will be me!

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:17.260
Now, the battle resumes!

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:19.420
Superstrength!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.970
Reversal!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:32.390
The Monarch, Dande, has arrived.

00:21:33.030 --> 00:21:35.180
With the trainer they seek
watching over them...

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:38.310
Who will win, Satoshi or Saito?!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.320
Next time, their battle will get
even more heated!

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:09.590
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.620 --> 00:23:13.080
This is bad, Satoshi!

00:23:13.080 --> 00:23:15.080
Mr. Dande’s here and watching!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:15.960
Yeah...

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:17.290
So I can’t lose this!

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:21.050
Fine then, let’s just destroy everything!

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:25.440
Your skill is worthy of respect—
and Kyodaimaxing!

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:29.560
